:: Orphanage Loft

<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
You are in the loft above the orphanage. A wide hall runs down the centre. Corridors leading to other rooms line the sides. Dusty boxes pile high.
<br>
<<if $loft_kylar>>
	An acrid smell wafts from one of the rooms.
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $loft_river is 1>>
	The smell of warm soup and fresh bread wafts from one of the rooms.
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $loft_doren is 1>>
	The comforting scent of books comes from the reading nook.
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $loft_gh gte 2>>
	Light filters through the bay window at the far back.
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $loft_sam is 1>>
	The scent of coffee wafts through the air.
	<br>
<</if>>
<br>
<<if $loft_spray isnot 1 and $spray lt $spraymax and $loft_kylar>>
	<<peppersprayicon>><<link [[Refill pepper spray|Orphanage Loft Spray]]>><<spray 1>><<set $loft_spray to 1>><</link>><<gspray>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $loft_river gte 1>>
	<<kitchenicon "range">><<link [[Secret kitchen|Orphanage Loft Kitchen]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $loft_doren is 1>>
	<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Reading nook|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $loft_gh gte 2>>
	<<baywindowicon>><<link [[Bay window|Orphanage Loft Bay Window]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $loft_sam is 1>>
	<<foodicon "coffee">><<link [[Coffee Pot|Orphanage Loft Coffee Pot]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<main_hall_icon>><<link [[Main hall (0:01)|Orphanage]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Orphanage Loft Spray

<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>><<wearProp "pepper spray">>
You enter the chemistry lab. Several beakers bubble away. A <<generateyv1>><<person1>><<person>> is running things. <<He>> hands you a freshly-made charge for your pepper spray.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Orphanage Loft Kitchen

<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<set $bus to "loft_kitchen">><<effects>>

You are in the kitchen in the orphanage loft, hidden away from Bailey.
<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	The orphans left a stew slow cooking overnight.
<<elseif Time.dayState is "dawn">>
	Orphans are arriving for breakfast.
<<elseif Time.dayState is "dusk">>
	The orphans are tidying up, cleaning pots and wiping away spilled flour.
<<else>>
	An orphan stirs a large, sweet-smelling pot, while others knead dough.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<robinorphanagekitchen>>

<<if Object.keys($loftIngredients).length gte 1>>
	<<for _i range Object.keys($loftIngredients)>>
		<<if $loftIngredients[_i] lte 0>>
			<<if $recipeMade and setup.foodstuff[$recipeMade].recipe?.ingredients.includes(_i)>>
				<span class="red">You used the last of the <<print setup.foodstuff[_i].plural>>.</span>
				<br>
			<</if>>
			<<run delete $loftIngredients[_i]>>
		<<else>>
			<span class="green">Some <<print setup.foodstuff[_i].plural>> were delivered here recently.</span> There should be enough for <span class="gold"><<number $loftIngredients[_i]>> <<pluralise $loftIngredients[_i] "meal">></span>.
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</for>>
	<br>
	<<ingredientsSupplied `Object.keys($loftIngredients)`>>
<<else>>
	You can cook whatever you like here, but you'll need to supply your own ingredients.
	<br><br>
<</if>>

<<allowLewdIngredients>>
<<kitchenDisplay>>

<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Orphanage Loft]]>><<kitchenExit>><</link>>
<br>

:: Orphanage Loft Reading Nook
<<effects>>
You stand before the cosy reading nook, by a window. The shelves are filled with books, newspapers, and magazines. Bookmarks, flash cards, stationery, and craft supplies are stored in the drawers.
<br><br>
<<rng 5>>
<<switch $rng>>
	<<case 1>>The orphans gather around the reading nook, listening to a <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> read.
	<<case 2>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> quizzes a <<generatey2>><<person2>><<person>> with flash cards.
	<<case 3>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> <<= either("quietly","expressively")>> reads in the nook.
	<<case 4>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> falls asleep in the nook.
	<<default>>A group of orphans are doing arts and crafts.
<</switch>>

<<endevent>>
<br><br>
<<if !$daily.reading_nook>>
	<<link [[Read a reference book (0:30)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "reference">><<pass 30>><</link>><<gtiredness>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Read a comic book (0:20)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "comic">><<pass 20>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<lstress>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Read a novel (0:30)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "novel">><<pass 30>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<genglish>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Read a newspaper (0:20)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "newspaper">><<pass 20>><</link>><<gtiredness>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Read a magazine (0:20)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "magazine">><<pass 20>><</link>><<gtiredness>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Study with the flash cards (0:20)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "flashcards">><<pass 20>><</link>><<gtiredness>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Do arts and crafts (0:20)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "crafts">><<pass 20>><</link>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>><<gtiredness>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Practise writing (0:20)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "write">><<pass 20>><</link>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>><<gtiredness>><<genglish>>
	<br>
	<<if ($worn.lower.name !== "naked" and ($worn.lower.integrity lte (clothingData('lower',$worn.lower,'integrity_max')/5))) or 
			($worn.upper.name !== "naked" and ($worn.upper.integrity lte (clothingData('upper',$worn.upper,'integrity_max')/5))) or 
			($worn.under_upper.name !== "naked" and ($worn.under_upper.integrity lte (clothingData('under_upper',$worn.under_upper,'integrity_max')/5))) or 
			($worn.under_lower.name !== "naked" and ($worn.under_lower.integrity lte (clothingData('under_lower',$worn.under_lower,'integrity_max')/5)))>>
		<<link [[Fix your clothes|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "sew">><</link>><<ghousekeeping>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $tiredness gte 1700>>
		<<link [[Take a nap (0:15)|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2]]>><<set $phase to "nap">><<pass 15>><</link>><<lstress>><<ltiredness>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Orphanage Loft]]>><<kitchenExit>><</link>>

:: Orphanage Loft Reading Nook 2
<<effects>>
<<set $daily.reading_nook to 1>>
<<if $phase is "reference">>
	<<tiredness 10>>
	<<rng 5>>
	<<switch $rng>>
		<<case 1>>
			It's a cookbook that teaches simple recipes.
			<br><br>
			<<reading_nook_recipe>>
		<<case 2>>It's an encyclopedia. You learn something new. <<= either(`<<genglish>><<englishskill>>`, `<<ghistory>><<historyskill>>`, `<<gmaths>><<mathsskill>>`, `<<gscience>><<scienceskill>>`)>>
		<<case 3>>It's an atlas of world history. You learn something new. <<ghistory>><<historyskill>>
		<<case 4>>It's a dictionary. You learn something new. <<genglish>><<englishskill>>
		<<default>>It's an illustrated book on <<= either("zoology", "human evolution", "nature", "biodiversity")>>. You learn something new. <<gscience>><<scienceskill>>
	<</switch>>
<<elseif ["novel","comic"].includes($phase)>>
	<<tiredness 10>>
	<<if $phase is "novel">>
		<<englishskill>>
		<<rng 3>>
		<<switch $rng>>
			<<case 1>>It's really hard to get through.
			<<case 2>><<= either("The prose flows so smoothly", "It's such a page-turner")>> that you don't realise an hour has gone by.<<pass 60>>
			<<case 3>>It's so immersive that you lose track of time.<<pass 60>>
			<<default>>It's a light read.
		<</switch>>
	<<else>>
		<<stress -5>>
		<<rng 6>>
		<<switch $rng>>
			<<case 1>>It's really hard to get through.
			<<case 2>>The use of <<= either("colours", "composition")>> is mind-blowing.
			<<case 3>>The art style is <<= either("cute", "unique", "eye-catching", "beautiful", "gorgeous")>>.
			<<case 4>><<= either("The prose flows so smoothly", "It's such a page-turner")>> that you don't realise an hour has gone by.<<pass 60>>
			<<case 5>>It's so immersive that you lose track of time.<<pass 60>>
			<<default>>It's a light read.
		<</switch>>
	<</if>>
	<<rng 10>>
	<<switch $rng>>
		<<case 1>>It makes you stop and think for a while.<<pass 40>>
		<<case 2>>It gives you an existential crisis. <<gstress>><<stress 5>>
		<<case 3>>It makes you appreciate life more. <<lstress>><<stress -5>>
		<<case 4>>It bores you,<<= either(" but you keep going", "<<set _read_bored to true>> so you stop reading", " so you skim through it")>>.
		<<case 5>>It entertains you. You have a great time. <<lstress>><<stress -5>>
		<<case 6>>It cracks you up. You burst out laughing a few times. <<lstress>><<stress -5>>
		<<case 7>>You're on the edge of your seat the whole time. The plot twist blows your mind.
		<<case 8>>It's a comforting read. You smile as you imagine yourself living in the book's universe. <<lstress>><<stress -5>>
		<<case 9>>It's a tear-jerker. You cry as you put yourself in the character's shoes.
		<<default>>It's so <<= either("dystopian", "terrifying")>>. You feel <<= either("a sense of dread crawling into your skin", "chills running down your spine")>>.
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	<<if _read_bored isnot true>>
		The ending <<= either("is perfect.", "can't be better than this.", "is alright.", "could be better.", "leaves you with more questions than answers.", "is half-baked.", "is a letdown.")>>
	<<else>>
		You don't care about the ending.
	<</if>>
<<elseif $phase is "newspaper">>
	<<tiredness 10>>
	<<rng 4>>
	<<switch $rng>>
		<<case 1>>Your reading comprehension strengthens. <<genglish>><<englishskill>>
		<<case 2>>You feel more informed about the world. <<ghistory>><<historyskill>>
		<<case 3>>You have a better understanding of social, political, and economic issues. <<gmaths>><<mathsskill>>
		<<default>>Your scientific literacy improves. <<gscience>><<scienceskill>>
	<</switch>>
<<elseif $phase is "magazine">>
	<<tiredness 10>>
	<<rng 3>>
	<<switch $rng>>
		<<case 1>>There's a cooking recipe being featured on this print. <<reading_nook_recipe>>
		<<case 2>>You feel more up-to-date with the current <<= either("fashion trends", "popular musicians", "popular artists")>>.
		<<default>>You read an interview about a <<= either("famous", "popular")>> <<= either("artist", "band", "musician")>>. It's <<= either("entertaining and insightful. <<lstress>><<stress -6>>", "dull and boring.")>>
	<</switch>>
<<elseif $phase is "flashcards">>
	<<tiredness 10>>
	You study using flash cards. You feel your memorisation is getting better.<<= either(`<<gggenglish>><<englishskill 18>>`, `<<ggghistory>><<historyskill 18>>`, `<<gggmaths>><<mathsskill 18>>`, `<<gggscience>><<scienceskill 18>>`)>>
<<elseif $phase is "write">>
	<<tiredness 10>><<englishskill>>
	You practise writing <<= either("poems","short stories")>>. It turns out <<=("awful","so-so","alright","great","amazing")>>.
<<elseif $phase is "nap">>
	<<tiredness -12>>
	You snuggle up and doze off, giving in to the sleepiness weighing on your eyes. You wake up later feeling refreshed and well-rested. <<lstress>><<stress -5>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -5>>
	<<if $englishtrait gte 3>>
		<<cleareventpool>>
		<<addinlineevent "readingorphans" 1>>
		<<generatey1>><<generatey2>>
		<br><br>
		You notice some orphans gather around you. One of them, a <<person1>><<person>> asks, "Good <<= (Time.hour lt 12 and Time.hour gt 5) ? `morning` : (Time.hour lte 17 and Time.hour gt 12) ? `afternoon` : `evening`>>! We were just wondering if you could read us a book?"
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Accept (0:20)|Reading Nook Orphans]]>><<pass 20>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>><<ghope>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Refuse|Reading Nook Orphans]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
		<<set _hide_links to 1>>
		<</addinlineevent>>
		<<runeventpool>>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $phase is "crafts">>
	<<tiredness 10>>
	Using the supplies in the drawers, you
	<<rng 4>>
	<<switch $rng>>
		<<case 1>>
			make some <<= either ("crochet crafts", "knit crafts", "bead crafts", "clay crafts", "felt crafts", "charms", "accessories", "pipe cleaner crafts", "papier-mâché crafts")>>.
		<<case 2>>
			<<= either(`<<wearProp "paper sheet">>`,`<<wearProp "scissors">>`)>>
			create some <<= either ("bookmarks", "origami")>>.
		<<case 3>>
			<<= either(`<<wearProp "paintbrush">>paint a picture`,`<<wearProp "pencil">>draw a sketch`)>>.
		<<default>>
			<<wearProp "rag">>
			embroider patterns on a piece of fabric.
	<</switch>>
		It's therapeutic. <<lstress>><<stress -5>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -5>>
<<elseif $phase is "sew">>
	<<housekeeping 5>>
	<<outfitChecks>>

	<<silently>>
	<<set _equip to []>>
	<<for _tatteredOutfit range Object.keys($worn)>>
		<<if _tatteredOutfit is "genitals" or $worn[_tatteredOutfit].name is "naked" or $worn[_tatteredOutfit].integrity is undefined>>
			<<continue>>
		<</if>>

		<<if $worn[_tatteredOutfit].integrity lte clothingData(_tatteredOutfit,$worn[_tatteredOutfit],'integrity_max')/5>>
			<<run _equip.push(_tatteredOutfit)>>
		<</if>>
	<</for>>

	<<set _items to []>>
	<<for _i to 0; _i lt _equip.length; _i++>>
		<<run _items.push($worn[_equip[_i]].name)>>
	<</for>>

	<<set _itemListText to formatList(_items, "and", true)>>
	<</silently>>

	<<if $housekeeping gte 800>>
		<<pass 15>>
		<<for _i to 0; _i lt _equip.length; _i++>>
			<<set $worn[_equip[_i]].integrity = clothingData(_equip[_i],$worn[_equip[_i]],'integrity_max')>>
			<<set $_slot to _equip[_i]>>
		<</for>>
		<<if _equip.length is 1>>
			You meticulously sew your tattered _itemListText. Now <<itis $_slot>> good as new.
		<<else>>
			You meticulously sew your tattered _itemListText. Now they're good as new.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $housekeeping gte 500>>
		<<pass 30>>
		<<for _i to 0; _i lt _equip.length; _i++>>
			<<set $worn[_equip[_i]].integrity = clothingData(_equip[_i],$worn[_equip[_i]],'integrity_max')>>
			<<set $_slot to _equip[_i]>>
		<</for>>
		<<if _equip.length is 1>>
			You sew your tattered _itemListText. It takes you some time, but now <<itis $_slot>> good as new.
		<<else>>
			You sew your tattered _itemListText. It takes you some time, but now they're good as new.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<rng 3>>
		<<switch $rng>>
			<<case 1>>
				<<pass 45>>
				<<for _i to 0; _i lt _equip.length; _i++>>
					<<set $worn[_equip[_i]].integrity = clothingData(_equip[_i],$worn[_equip[_i]],'integrity_max')>>
				<</for>>

				You try to sew your tattered _itemListText. It takes you a lot longer than you thought.
			<<case 2>>
				<<pass 45>>
				<<for _i to 0; _i lt _equip.length; _i++>>
					<<set $worn[_equip[_i]].integrity -= $worn[_equip[_i]].integrity/2>>
					<<if $worn[_equip[_i]].integrity lt 1>>
						<<generalRuined _equip[_i]>>
					<</if>>
					<<set $_slot to _equip[_i]>>
				<</for>>

				You try to sew your tattered _itemListText.
				<<if _equip.length is 1>>
					Unfortunately, your attempted fix just makes <<it $_slot>> worse. Your _itemListText <<is $_slot>> even more tattered now.
				<<else>>
					Unfortunately, your attempted fix just make them worse. Your _itemListText are even more tattered now.
				<</if>>
			<<default>>
				<<pass 15>>
				<<for _i to 0; _i lt _equip.length; _i++>>
					<<set $worn[_equip[_i]].integrity = $worn[_equip[_i]].integrity + clothingData(_equip[_i],$worn[_equip[_i]],'integrity_max')/10>>
				<</for>>
				You try to fix your _itemListText meticulously. You get a bit done.
		<</switch>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if !_hide_links>>
	<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Reading Nook Orphans
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<famegood 10>><<hope 1>>
	"Thank you!" They smile and sit down, listening to you read. <<= either("Your delivery keeps them hooked and engaged", "You act out the scenes and put on silly voices, entertaining them greatly")>>. After finishing the book, you quiz them about it, and they're happy to participate. You have a great time.<<lstress>><<stress -5>><<gtiredness>><<tiredness 10>>
<<else>>
	You shake your head.
	<br><br>
	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"Sorry, I'm afraid not."
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		"No. Sorry not sorry."
	<<else>>
		"Sorry, but not today."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	The <<person2>><<person>> reassures you. "It's okay. We understand. Have a nice day!"
	<br><br>
	"Goodbye," the group unanimously says. They scurry away.
<</if>>

<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft Reading Nook]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Orphanage Loft Bay Window
<<effects>>

You stand before the bay window. It rises above you. The latch on the central window holds firm.
<<if $loft_gh is 3>>
	The quilts, padded by the duvets beneath, look comfy. Cushions and pillows are scattered across the bay. The wind chime sways gently.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if Time.hour lte 22>>
	<<switch random(1,4)>>
		<<case 1>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> watches over the garden below.
		<<case 2>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> chats with a <<generatey2>><<person2>><<person>> while sitting on the window board<<if $loft_gh is 3>>, hugging a pillow in <<person1>><<his>> chest<</if>>.
		<<case 3>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> basks <<= Time.dayState is "night" ? "beneath the moonlight" : "in the sunlight">>, dozing off.
		<<default>>Some orphans gather near the windows, peering out and pointing excitedly at something in the forest.
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
You open the window and perch on the edge of the sill, dangling your feet in the air.
<br><br>

<<loft_window_options>>

:: Orphanage Loft Bay Window Preen
<<effects>>

<<if $plucked>>
	You try to preen your wings, but Gwylan left nothing loose. You're thoroughly plucked already.
<<elseif $daily.birdSelfPreen is undefined>>
	<<set $daily.birdSelfPreen to 1>>
	You preen your wings. It's harder doing this alone.
	<<set _selfFeatherNum to random(1,2)>>
	<<switch _selfFeatherNum>>
		<<case 1>>One of your loose feathers has fallen out. <span class="teal">You take it.</span>
		<<case 2>>A couple of your loose feathers have fallen out. <span class="teal">You take them.</span>
	<</switch>>
	<<set $bird.materials.feathers += _selfFeatherNum>>
	<<wearProp "pc feather" "hair">>
<<else>>
	You preen your wings. There's no more loose feathers to remove for now, but it makes you feel better regardless.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<loft_window_options>>

:: Orphanage Loft Bay Window Sing
<<effects>>

<<if $harpy gte 6>>
	<<transform bird 1>>
	<<print either(
		"Your powerful, clear voice pierces the air and subdues every creature it can reach, even the most finicky. The forest yields to you.",
		"Your deep and gentle voice soothes all the sorrows of the world. The forest seems a little more peaceful.",
		"Your glorious song beckons to a distant land. The trees rattle and the leaves rustle as if heeding your call.",
		"You hum in the wind, letting it carry your song across the vast expanse of the sky. The trees make way and blossoms bloom even more beautifully wherever it passes.",
		"Your ballad graces the very air. Nature holds its breath in reverence for you.",
		"Your melody rides the air as though the sky welcomes it home.",
		"Your voice drips like honeyed song through the air. Every note pulls at the heart like a siren's call.",
		"Each note from your throat feels bright enough to stir the skies. Even the breeze seems to dance to your melody."
	)>><<trauma -6>><<ltrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<cleareventpool>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_birds" 1>>
		Your melodic tune attracts <<= Time.dayState is "night" ? "an owl, and it perches beside you on the sill. Its hoot backs your song" : "a flock of songbirds. They gather around you, adding their chirping as accompaniment">>.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<if $seabird_lullaby gte 2 and !$weekly.seabird_sing>>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_lullaby" .01>>
			<<set $weekly.seabird_sing to true>>
			On a whim, you hum the six familiar notes of the <span class="teal">Seabird's Lullaby</span>. Then, words slip from your lips in the most natural way. Everything is silent, except for your voice. <<if Time.hour gte 23>>It drifts through the air, carrying even the weariest of souls to sleep.<</if>>
			<br><br>
			A soft singing echoes from the forest.
			<<if $gwylan.hunting gte 2 and $hypnosis_traits.devotion gt 0 and !isGwylanAbsent()>>
				<<silently>><<gwylanWillpowerDifficulty>><</silently>>
				It evokes a strange, compelling feeling, and suddenly, you feel an urge to venture deeper into the forest.
					<<if $willpowerSuccess>>
						You shake your head and push the thought aside.
					<<else>>
						You sink deeper into the trance. <<hypnosisText "Guilt sets in as you recall the duties you've neglected.">><<trauma 6>><<gtrauma>>
					<</if>>
			<<elseif isGwylanAbsent() is "nobody">>
				It sounds like nobody. You shake your head. You hear nothing.
			<<else>>
				It sounds like Gwylan. Your voices join and weave into a duet.
			<</if>>
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<if Time.hour gte 21>>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_orphan_lull" .5>>
			<<generatey1>><<person1>>
			Another orphan falls asleep nearby. You lower your voice into a soothing coo.
			<br><br>
			You wake <<him>> up after a moment and suggest <<he>> go to bed.
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $dissociation gte 1 and $hallucinations gte 2 and Time.dayState is "night">>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_trauma" 1>>
			You pour your sorrow and distress into the cold night. Darkness shrouds your lonely tune, seemingly wanting to swallow you whole.
			<<if Weather.bloodMoon>>
				For a moment, the red moon looks just like an eye, boring into you with malicious intent. Something is coming for you. <span class="red">You open your mouth, and find yourself unable to sing.</span><<trauma 10>><<ggtrauma>>
				<<set $daily.no_sing to true>>
			<</if>>
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<if Weather.bloodMoon and Time.dayState is "night">>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_blood" .7>>
			<<set $daily.no_sing to true>>
			<<set _no_options to true>>
			The deep red moonlight envelopes you, painting everything in red. Your voice trembles, a feeling of dread filling your chest.
			<br><br>
			Something terrible is near.
			<br><br>
			It had arrived.
			<br><br>
			<span class="red">First, no sound leaves your throat.
			<br><br>
			Second, you no longer hear anything at all.
			<br><br>
			Third, red swarms your vision, until you can't see anymore. There's so much blood.</span><<trauma 10>><<ggtrauma>>
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $world_corruption_soft gte 99 and $hallucinations gte 2 and Time.dayState is "night">>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_snuffed" 1>>
			Your surroundings suddenly become darker, tendrils of darkness closing on you.
			<br><br>
			You no longer hear your own singing. You scream. That is snuffed too. <span class="red">Your voice is stolen from you.</span><<trauma 20>><<gggtrauma>>
			<br><br>
			The night is eerily quiet. There's no sound except for your heavy breathing.
			<<set $daily.no_sing to true>>
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $loft_gh is 3>>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_chimes" 1>>
			The wind gently sways the wind chimes, creating tinkling sounds that blend with your voice, forming a harmonious symphony.
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_instrument" .7>>
		<<generatey1>><<person1>>
		A <<person>> sits by you, holding
		<<if random(1,50) is 50>>
			<<print either("a crwth", "a citole", "a pibgorn", "a cittern", "a concertina", "a bone flute", "a hurdy-gurdy", "an Anglo-Saxon lyre")>> in <<his>> hand.
			<br><br>
			You pause your song briefly, and curiously examine <<his>> instrument. It's a rare sight to see one of these.
		<<else>>
			<<print either("a harmonica", "a guitar", "a clarinet", "a hand drum", "a violin", "a lyre", "an ukulele", "a kalimba", "a saxophone")>> in <<his>> hand.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<He>> offers you a smile and wordlessly adds <<his>> music to your singing. <<He>> tries <<his>> best to keep up with you.
		<br><br>
		By the end, <<his>> face is flushed with excitement. <<He>> looks at you with admiration, as if you are <<his>> muse.<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_wolves" 1>>
		You can hear howling from afar. <<if $wolfpackleader is 1>> Your legion of wolves sing back to you in their own way.<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_longing" 1>>
		The sky sends forth a powerful gust of wind, as if to express its longing for you. <<if $transformationParts.bird.wings isnot "hidden">>Your wings flutter, each feather caressed by the breeze.<</if>> You yearn to touch the sky again. <<if $plucked>>But your wings cannot carry you into the sky, at least not yet.<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "default" 1>>
		Your song rides the wind, wandering far beyond the skyline.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<runeventpool>>
<<else>>
	You sing to the forest, and it responds in kind with
	<<if Weather.precipitation isnot "none">>
		<<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
			a passing breeze that carries the earthy smell of damp woods.
		<<else>>
			a gust of wind that lands a snowflake on your nose. You sneeze.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif Time.season is "autumn">>
		a soothing breeze that smells like decaying leaves and ripe fruits.
	<<elseif Time.season is "summer">>
		a fresh breeze with a hint of spice and sweetness from the tree resin melted by the sun's sheer intensity.
	<<else>>
		a gentle zephyr with the scent of crisp pines and blooming flowers.
	<</if>>
	<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<cleareventpool>>

	<<if Time.dayState is "night" and !Weather.bloodMoon and !Weather.isOvercast>>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_moonlight" 1>>
			The moon rests high in the night sky, gently casting its silver hue upon you.
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $dissociation gte 1>>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_sorrow" .7>>
			<<set $daily.no_sing to true>>
			Your singing stops abruptly. A lump forms in your throat as the weight of everything has happened crashes down onto you. You cover your face.
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<if Weather.bloodMoon and Time.dayState is "night">>
		<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_dread" 1>>
			<<set $daily.no_sing to true>>
			You pause, and look up to the sky. The blood moon bears down on you, filling your vision with red.
			<br><br>
			<span class="red">Suddenly, you don't want to sing anymore.</span>
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_clap" 1>>
		<<generatey1>><<person1>>
		A young orphan joins your side. <<He>> claps to your song in encouragement.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_sing_wave" 1>>
		Some orphans see you from the garden and wave at you.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<runeventpool>>
<</if>>

<br><br>
<<loft_window_options>>

:: Orphanage Loft Bay Window Watch
<<effects>>

You watch the forest.
<br><br>
<<if $transformationParts.traits.sharpEyes isnot "disabled">>
	With your sharp eyesight, you can see
	<<switch random(1,13)>>
		<<case 1>>seasonal flowers in full bloom across the outskirts.
		<<case 2>>ripe fruits hanging from distant trees.
		<<case 3>>a fox burying a bird egg in the distance.
		<<case 4>>a lone wolf running deeper into the forest, until it disappears into a cave.
		<<case 5>>smoke rising from somewhere deep within the forest.
		<<case 6>>a lone figure disappearing deeper into the forest.
		<<case 7>>branches swaying despite the still air.
		<<case 8>>a rabbit darting through the undergrowth.
		<<case 9>>a narrow trail winding through the forest.
		<<case 10>>a squirrel leaping between branches.
		<<case 11>>a deer grazing near the forest edge.
		<<case 12>>ripples spreading across a hidden pond.
		<<default>>a flock of birds circling above the trees.
	<</switch>>
	<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<<else>>
	Lush greenery stretches as far as the eye can see. You can spot a corner of the forest lake. You feel at ease.<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<cleareventpool>>

<<if $transformationParts.traits.sharpEyes isnot "disabled">>
	<<addinlineevent "forest_watch_shop" .01>>
		You notice a strange, castle-like shop cradled in the treeline.<<if $forest_shop_intro is 1>> It's the forest shop.<</if>>
		<br><br>
		From here, you can peer through the top window of the building. <<= isGwylanAbsent() is "nobody" ? "Nobody is there.": "A silhouette paces back and forth. As if sensing your gaze, it pauses abruptly in front of the window, staring back at you.">>
		<br><br>
		You look away.
	<</addinlineevent>>
<</if>>

<<addinlineevent "forest_watch_gun" .2>>
	A distant gunshot rings through the forest. Moments later, a flock of startled birds takes flight above the trees.
<</addinlineevent>>

<<addinlineevent "forest_watch_misc" 10>>
	<<switch random(1,7)>>
		<<case 1>>
			<<if $loft_gh is 3>>
				<<print either(
					"The curtains billow softly beside you.",
					"The quilts sink comfortably beneath your weight.",
					"The blankets bunch beneath your shifting weight.",
					"The curtains flutter softly against the wooden frame.",
					"Loose fabric rustles quietly in the breeze."
				)>>
			<<else>>
				The scent of evergreen lingers in the air.
			<</if>>
		<<case 2>>
			<<if Weather.name is "thunderstorm">>
				A cold storm blankets the forest in darkness. You sit alone by the open window, feeling stray droplets patter softly against your legs as lightning splits the sky.
			<<elseif Weather.precipitation isnot "none">>
				<<= Weather.precipitation is "rain" ? "Raindrops patter gently against your dangling legs." : "Snow gathers along the window sill.">>
			<<else>>
				The <<= Time.dayState is "night" ? "moonlight caresses": Time.dayState is "dusk" ? "sunset washes across" : "sun warms">> your skin as you lean against the open frame.
			<</if>>
		<<case 3>>
			<<if $loft_river is 1>>
				The smell of soup drifts from the kitchen.
			<<else>>
				A calm silence settles over the orphanage.
			<</if>>
		<<case 4>>
			<<if Weather.bloodMoon>>
				The blood moon dyes the trees red. The forest is eerily silent.
			<<elseif Time.dayState is "night">>
				<<print either(
					"The night forest hums with unseen life.",
					"The moon hangs silently above the forest.",
					"Moonlight washes the bay window silver."
				)>>
			<<else>>
				Warm light pools across the loft floor.
			<</if>>
		<<case 5>>
			<<if Time.season is "spring">>
				Spring flowers visible beyond the trees.
			<<elseif Time.season is "winter">>
				Snow gathers upon the evergreen boughs.
			<<elseif Time.season is "summer">>
				Cicadas humming outside.
			<<else>>
				Fallen leaves blow through the open window.
			<</if>>
		<<case 6>>
			<<if $harpy gte 6 and $transformationParts.bird.wings isnot "hidden">>
				<<print either(
					"Your feathers flutter loosely in the breeze.",
					"A warm breeze slips through your feathers.",
					"The wind teases through your feathers.",
					"The open sky stirs a longing within you.",
					"You stretch your wings."
				)>>
			<<else>>
				Fallen leaves spiral through the forest air.
			<</if>>
		<<default>><<print either(
		"The wind rustles the trees.",
		"Birds migrating overhead.",
		"Wolves howling far away.",
		"The forest canopy sways gently below.",
		"Birds flit between the tree branches.",
		"Fallen needles blanket the forest floor beneath the evergreens.",
		"The orphans chatter quietly around the bay.",
		"Birdsong echoes from somewhere beyond the trees.",
		"The forest stretches endlessly beneath the horizon."
		)>>
	<</switch>>
<</addinlineevent>>

<<addinlineevent "forest_watch_idle" 1>>
	Nothing seems out of the ordinary.
<</addinlineevent>>

<<runeventpool>>
<br><br>
<<loft_window_options>>

:: Orphanage Loft Coffee Pot
<<effects>>

You walk over to the coffee pot. The rich aroma greets you.
<br><br>
<<switch random(1,6)>>
	<<case 1>>Other orphans are standing around the machine, brewing themself a drink.
	<<case 2>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> is making coffee.
	<<case 3>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> is picking out what to drink.
	<<case 4>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> looks ready to faint, but perks right up after taking a sip of coffee.
	<<case 5>>A <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> is tossing a bunch of sugar in <<his>> coffee, after having a sip, you can tell <<he>> put too much.
	<<default>>You watch a <<generatey1>><<person1>><<person>> tell off a <<generatey2>><<person2>><<person>> for drinking too much coffee.
<</switch>>
<br><br>

<<if $daily.loftcoffee isnot 1>>
	<<foodicon "coffee">><<link [[Make a cup of coffee|Orphanage Loft Coffee Pot Drink]]>><<endevent>><<set $daily.loftcoffee to 1>><<pass 5>><<stress -3>><<tiredness -4>><</link>><<lstress>><<ltiredness>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<span class="blue">You've had your fill for today.</span>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Orphanage Loft]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Orphanage Loft Coffee Pot Drink
<<effects>>
<<wearProp "coffee">>
<<set _coffee to either("mocha", "latte", "caramel latte", "white chocolate mocha", "flat white", "caramel iced latte")>>
You make yourself a _coffee. The scent of freshly brewed coffee fills the air.
<br><br>
<<switch random(1,6)>>
	<<case 1>>It tastes delicious, you can tell Sam picked out some good beans for you.
	<<case 2>>It's a bit bitter, but you drink it anyway.
	<<case 3>>You can taste all the different notes in the coffee.
	<<case 4>>There's a slight fruity flavour to the coffee, it's tasty.
	<<case 5>>The coffee isn't that strong this time, you wonder if you didn't put enough grounds in the machine.
	<<default>>You feel a bit jittery. Maybe it wasn't a good idea to make yourself a coffee. At least the taste is good.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if Time.betweenHours(6,11)>>
	<<set _daytime to "morning">>
<<elseif Time.betweenHours(12,17)>>
	<<set _daytime to "afternoon">>
<<elseif Time.betweenHours(18,20)>>
	<<set _daytime to "evening">>
<<else>>
	<<set _daytime to "nighttime">>
<</if>>
You finish the drink, and clean up after yourself. You feel refreshed after the _daytime coffee.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft Coffee Pot]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
